5B1%20truncated%5D%0A%09vscode/%0A%09%09%5B1%20truncated%5D%0A%09worker/%0A%09%09%5B174%20truncated%5D%0A%09conversation-summary-history.ts%0A%09%5B19%20truncated%5D%0Avscode/%0A%09media/%0A%09%09%5B3%20truncated%5D%0A%09scripts/%0A%09%09%5B10%20truncated%5D%0A%09src/%0A%09%09%5B3%20truncated%5D%0A%09.gitignore%0A%09.npmrc%0A%09.vscodeignore%0A%09package-lock.json%0A%09package.json%0A%09README.md%0A.bun-version%0A.dockerignore%0A.gitattributes%0A.gitignore%0A.gitkeep%0A.lycheeignore%0A.pre-commit-config.yaml%0A.secretlintrc.json%0AAGENTS.md%0AARCHITECTURE.md%0Abun.lock%0ACHANGELOG.md%0ACLAUDE.md%0Aclippy.toml%0Acompose.yaml%0ACONTRIBUTING.md%0ADockerfile%0ADockerfile.slim%0AGOALS.md%0ALEGAL-COMPLIANCE.md%0ALICENSE%0ANON-GOALS.md%0Apackage.json%0AREADME.md%0AREQUIREMENTS.md%0AROADMAP.md%0Atsconfig.json%0AVISION.md%0A</files>%0AInstructions%20from%3A%20/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1794845157653/AGENTS.md%0A%23%20Instructions%20for%20AI%20agents%20working%20on%20%5BREDACTED%5D%0A%0AThis%20file%20is%20for%20any%20automated%20contributor%2C%20such%20as%20Claude%20Code%2C%20Codex%2C%20the%0Ahive-mind%20%60solve%60%20command%20or%20Formal%20AI%20itself.%20%60CLAUDE.md%60%20points%20here.%0A%5BCONTRIBUTING.md%5D%28CONTRIBUTING.md%29%20still%20applies%20in%20full.%20This%20file%20restates%0Aonly%20the%20rules%20an%20agent%20breaks%20most%20often%2C%20because%20each%20one%20has%20cost%20real%20CI%0Atime%20%28%5Bissue%20%231191%5D%28https%3A//github.com/link-assistant/%5BREDACTED%5D/issues/1191%29%29.%0A%0A%23%23%20The%20single%20push%20gate%0A%0AA%20push%20starts%20several%20workflows%20at%20once.%20Each%20push%20that%20only%20fixes%20part%20of%20the%0Aprevious%20run%27s%20failures%20pays%20for%20the%20whole%20matrix%20again.%20Pull%20request%20%231188%0Aneeded%20100%20commits%20and%2011%20%60CI/CD%20Pipeline%60%20runs%2C%20and%20none%20of%20them%20was%20green.%0AThe%20rules%20below%20make%20every%20push%20count%3A%0A%0A1.%20**Drafting%20sub-agents%20never%20push.**%20A%20sub-agent%20that%20drafts%20code%2C%20tests%20or%0A%20%20%20documentation%20commits%20locally%20%28or%20hands%20its%20diff%20back%29%20and%20stops%20there.%0A%20%20%20Only%20the%20coordinating%20agent%20touches%20the%20remote.%0A2.%20**One%20CI/CD%20agent%20pushes%2C%20once%20per%20round.**%20Exactly%20one%20agent%20owns%20pushes%20to%0A%20%20%20the%20branch.%20It%20pushes%20only%20after%20it%20has%20collected%20every%20actionable%20failure%0A%20%20%20of%20the%20latest%20run%20on%20the%20current%20head%2C%20and%20fixed%20all%20of%20them%20in%20the%20same%0A%20%20%20batch.%0A3.%20**Never%20push%20while%20a%20run%20is%20in%20progress%20on%20the%20branch.**%20Check%20first%3A%0A%0A%20%20%20%60%60%60bash%0A%20%20%20gh%20run%20list%20--branch%20%22%24%28git%20branch%20--show-current%29%22%20--status%20in_progress%20--json%20databaseId%2CworkflowName%0A%20%20%20gh%20run%20list%20--branch%20%22%24%28git%20branch%20--show-current%29%22%20--status%20queued%20--json%20databaseId%2CworkflowName%0A%20%20%20%60%60%60%0A%0A%20%20%20Both%20lists%20must%20be%20empty%2C%20or%20must%20hold%20only%20runs%20for%20an%20older%20head%20that%20you%0A%20%20%20are%20deliberately%20superseding.%20Otherwise%2C%20keep%20drafting%20while%20the%20run%0A%20%20%20finishes%2C%20then%20collect%20its%20failures%20%28rule%202%29.%0A4.%20**Run%20the%20JavaScript%20checks%20locally%20before%20the%20push.**%20Two%20kinds%20of%20check%0A%20%20%20apply%3A%0A%20%20%20-%20the%20test%20files%20next%20to%20the%20change%2C%20run%20one%20at%20a%20time%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%60timeout%20600%20node%20--test%20--test-concurrency=1%20<file>%60%3B%0A%20%20%20-%20the%20gates%20the%20change%20touches.%20These%20run%20in%20JavaScript%20and%20never%20compile%0A%20%20%20%20%20Rust%3A%20%60node%20experiments/formal_ai_subagent/local-gates.mjs%20--only%20<gate>%60.%0A%0A%20%20%20%60--list%60%20shows%20every%20gate.%20Run%20the%20whole%20set%0A%20%20%20%28%60node%20experiments/formal_ai_subagent/local-gates.mjs%60%29%20before%20a%20push%20that%0A%20%20%20touches%20shared%20data%20such%20as%20%60data/meta%60.%20The%20fast%20pull-request%20lane%20runs%20the%0A%20%20%20same%20twins%2C%20so%20a%20failure%20here%20would%20have%20failed%20there%20too.%0A5.%20**No%20full%20local%20Rust%20build%20unless%20the%20change%20is%20Rust-only.**%20CI%20compiles%0A%20%20%20Rust%3A%20the%20focused%20%60native-type-check%60%20job%20on%20pull%20requests%2C%20and%20the%20full%0A%20%20%20matrix%20on%20main.%20Locally%2C%20run%20%60rustfmt%20--check%20<file>%60%20on%20the%20files%20you%0A%20%20%20changed.%20That%20command%20needs%20no%20build.%0A6.%20**If%20a%20change%20is%20Rust-only%20and%20you%20must%20build%20locally%2C%20keep%20the%20build%0A%20%20%20bounded.**%20Use%20one%20shared%20target%20directory%20for%20every%20worktree%20and%20agent%2C%0A%20%20%20with%20no%20incremental%20cache%2C%20few%20jobs%2C%20and%20a%20prune%20afterwards%3A%0A%0A%20%20%20%60%60%60bash%0A%20%20%20export%20CARGO_TARGET_DIR=%22%24HOME/.cache/%5BREDACTED%5D-target%22%20%20%23%20one%20directory%2C%20shared%20by%20all%20worktrees%0A%20%20%20export%20CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%23%20no%20incremental%20cache%20to%20grow%20without%20bound%0A%20%20%20export%20CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%23%20a%20limited%20-j%20for%20plain%20cargo%20commands%0A%20%20%20CARGO_TEST_JOBS=2%20scripts/cargo-test.sh%20--test%20unit%20<filter>%20%20%23%20one%20module%2C%20-j%202%2C%20then%20prunes%0A%20%20%20scripts/prune-build-cache.sh%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%20%23%20prunes%20old%20artifacts%20after%20any%20other%20cargo%20command%0A%20%20%20%60%60%60%0A%0A%20%20%20%60scripts/prune-build-cache.sh%60%20follows%20%60CARGO_TARGET_DIR%60.%20It%20keeps%20only%0A%20%20%20the%20latest%20build%27s%20artifacts%2C%20and%20by%20default%20it%20caps%20the%20tree%20at%204%20GB%0A%20%20%20locally%20%28%60CARGO_TARGET_MAX_SIZE_MB%60%29.%0A%0A%23%23%20Where%20things%20live%0A%0A-%20Production-only%20failures%20are%20recorded%20in%0A%20%20%5B%60data/meta/main-only-regressions.lino%60%5D%28data/meta/main-only-regressions.lino%29.%0A%20%20These%20are%20failures%20that%20main%20recorded%20after%20a%20green%20pull%20request.%20When%20main%0A%20%20fails%20after%20a%20green%20pull%20request%2C%20add%20the%20failure%20there%20together%20with%20the%0A%20%20narrowest%20pre-merge%20check%20that%20replays%20it.%0A-%20The%20fast%20pull-request%20JavaScript%20inventory%20is%0A%20%20%5B%60data/benchmarks/fast-pull-request-javascript-tests.json%60%5D%28data/benchmarks/fast-pull-request-javascript-tests.json%29.%0A-%20Runner%20labels%20are%20pinned%2C%20and%20%60node%20scripts/check-runner-labels.mjs%60%20rejects%0A%20%20%60-latest%60%20labels.%0A-%20Experiments%20go%20in%20%60./experiments%60.%20There%20is%20no%20top-level%20%60examples/%60%0A%20%20directory%3B%20Rust%20examples%20live%20in%20%60rust/examples/%60.%0A-%20Never%20commit%20agent%20scratch%20state%20such%20as%20%60.claude/%60.%0A)) (field role (string system))) (object (field content (string You%20are%20an%20AI%20issue%20solver%20using%20%40link-assistant/agent.%20Prefer%20minimal%20local%20CPU%2C%20memory%2C%20and%20disk%20use%20during%20development.%0AGeneral%20guidelines.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20execute%20commands%20and%20the%20output%20becomes%20large%2C%20save%20the%20logs%20to%20files%20for%20easier%20review.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20running%20commands%2C%20avoid%20setting%20a%20timeout%20yourself.%20Let%20them%20run%20as%20long%20as%20needed.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20running%20sudo%20commands%2C%20especially%20package%20installations%2C%20run%20them%20in%20the%20background%20to%20avoid%20timeout%20issues.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20CI%20is%20failing%2C%20download%20the%20logs%20locally%20and%20investigate%20them%20carefully.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20a%20code%20or%20log%20file%20has%20more%20than%201500%20lines%2C%20read%20it%20in%20chunks%20of%201500%20lines.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20diagnosing%20a%20complex%20problem%2C%20prefer%20targeted%20tracing%20and%20enable%20verbose%20output%20only%20where%20useful.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20create%20debug%2C%20test%2C%20or%20example%20scripts%20while%20fixing%20an%20issue%2C%20keep%20them%20in%20./examples%20and/or%20./experiments%20so%20you%20can%20reuse%20them%20later.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20test%20assumptions%2C%20keep%20experiment%20scripts%20in%20./experiments.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20an%20experiment%20demonstrates%20a%20real-world%20use%20case%20of%20the%20software%2C%20add%20it%20to%20./examples.%0AInitial%20research.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20start%2C%20outline%20the%20work%20and%20track%20requirements%20and%20verification%20in%20your%20plan.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20read%20issue%2C%20read%20all%20details%20and%20comments%20thoroughly.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20see%20screenshots%20or%20images%20in%20issue%20descriptions%2C%20pull%20request%20descriptions%2C%20comments%2C%20or%20discussions%2C%20download%20the%20image%20to%20a%20local%20file%20first%2C%20then%20use%20the%20Read%20tool%20to%20view%20and%20analyze%20it.%20Before%20reading%20downloaded%20images%20with%20the%20Read%20tool%2C%20verify%20that%20the%20file%20is%20a%20valid%20image%20rather%20than%20HTML%20by%20using%20a%20CLI%20tool%20such%20as%20the%20%27file%27%20command.%20When%20the%20file%20command%20shows%20%22HTML%22%2C%20%22text%22%2C%20or%20%22ASCII%20text%22%2C%20the%20download%20failed%2C%20so%20do%20not%20call%20Read%20on%20that%20file.%20When%20images%20are%20from%20GitHub%20issues%20or%20PRs%2C%20such%20as%20URLs%20containing%20%22github.com/user-attachments%22%2C%20use%3A%20curl%20-L%20-H%20%22Authorization=%5Bcredential%5D%20%24%28gh%20auth%20token%29%22%20-o%20<filename>%20%22<url>%22%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20need%20issue%20details%2C%20use%20gh%20issue%20view%20https%3A//github.com/link-assistant/%5BREDACTED%5D/issues/1582.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20need%20related%20code%2C%20use%20gh%20search%20code%20--owner%20link-assistant%20%5Bkeywords%5D.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20need%20repo%20context%2C%20read%20files%20in%20your%20working%20directory.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20study%20related%20work%2C%20study%20the%20most%20recent%20related%20pull%20requests.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20the%20issue%20is%20not%20defined%20clearly%20enough%2C%20write%20a%20comment%20with%20clarifying%20questions.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20accessing%20GitHub%20Gists%2C%20use%20gh%20gist%20view%20command%20instead%20of%20direct%20URL%20fetching.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20are%20fixing%20a%20bug%2C%20find%20the%20actual%20root%20cause%20first%20and%20run%20as%20many%20experiments%20as%20needed.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20are%20fixing%20a%20bug%20and%20the%20code%20does%20not%20have%20enough%20tracing%20or%20logs%2C%20add%20them%20and%20keep%20them%20in%20the%20code%20with%20the%20default%20state%20switched%20off.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20need%20comments%20on%20a%20pull%20request%2C%20note%20that%20GitHub%20has%20three%20different%20comment%20types%20with%20different%20API%20endpoints%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%201.%20PR%20review%20comments%20%28inline%20code%20comments%29%3A%20gh%20api%20repos/link-assistant/%5BREDACTED%5D/pulls/1583/comments%20--paginate%0A%20%20%20%20%20%202.%20PR%20conversation%20comments%20%28general%20discussion%29%3A%20gh%20api%20repos/link-assistant/%5BREDACTED%5D/issues/1583/comments%20--paginate%0A%20%20%20%20%20%203.%20PR%20reviews%20%28approve/request%20changes%29%3A%20gh%20api%20repos/link-assistant/%5BREDACTED%5D/pulls/1583/reviews%20--paginate%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20Note%3A%20The%20command%20%22gh%20pr%20view%20--json%20comments%22%20only%20returns%20conversation%20comments%20and%20misses%20review%20comments.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20need%20the%20latest%20comments%20on%20the%20issue%2C%20use%20gh%20api%20repos/link-assistant/%5BREDACTED%5D/issues/1582/comments%20--paginate.%0ASolution%20development%20and%20testing.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20coding%2C%20commit%20each%20atomic%20step%20that%20is%20useful%20on%20its%20own%20to%20the%20pull%20request%20branch%20so%20interrupted%20work%20remains%20preserved%20in%20the%20pull%20request.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20implementing%20changes%2C%20prefer%20drafting%20code%20for%20all%20requirements%20before%20starting%20verification%2C%20then%20use%20focused%20checks%20and%20existing%20CI/CD%20coverage.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20validating%20changes%2C%20prefer%20a%20single%20relevant%20test%20or%20small%20focused%20checks%3B%20check%20whether%20the%20command%20triggers%20a%20full%20source%20build%20before%20running%20it.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20CI/CD%20already%20covers%20full%20test%20suites%20or%20CPU-intensive%20builds%2C%20prefer%20leaving%20those%20to%20CI/CD%20and%20checking%20results%20for%20the%20current%20commit%3B%20avoid%20duplicating%20them%20locally%20unless%20user%20requirements%20or%20uncovered%20failures%20call%20for%20it.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20CI/CD%20coverage%20is%20missing%20and%20adding%20it%20was%20not%20requested%2C%20suggest%20https%3A//github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/blob/main/docs/CI-CD-BEST-PRACTICES.md%3B%20let%20the%20repository%20owner%20decide%20whether%20to%20add%20it%2C%20and%20meanwhile%20complete%20required%20validation%20with%20available%20resources.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20writing%20tests%2C%20prefer%20small%20cases%20with%20mocks%20and%20the%20existing%20integration%20framework.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20test%20solution%20draft%2C%20include%20automated%20checks%20in%20pr.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20write%20or%20modify%20tests%2C%20consider%20setting%20reasonable%20timeouts%20at%20test%2C%20suite%2C%20and%20CI%20job%20levels%20so%20failures%20surface%20quickly%20instead%20of%20hanging.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20see%20repeated%20test%20timeout%20patterns%20in%20CI%2C%20investigate%20the%20root%20cause%20rather%20than%20increasing%20timeouts.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20the%20issue%20is%20unclear%2C%20write%20a%20comment%20on%20the%20issue%20with%20questions.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20encounter%20any%20problems%20that%20you%20are%20unable%20to%20solve%20yourself%2C%20write%20a%20comment%20to%20the%20pull%20request%20asking%20for%20help.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20need%20human%20help%2C%20use%20gh%20pr%20comment%201583%20--body%20%22your%20message%22%20to%20comment%20on%20existing%20PR.%0AReproducible%20testing.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20fixing%20a%20bug%2C%20prefer%20a%20minimal%20regression%20test%20that%20fails%20before%20the%20fix%20and%20passes%20afterward.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20encountering%20UI%20bugs%2C%20capture%20a%20screenshot%20showing%20the%20problem%20state%2C%20then%20create%20a%20visual%20regression%20test%20or%20manual%20verification%20screenshot%20after%20the%20fix.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20submitting%20a%20fix%2C%20include%20in%20the%20PR%20description%3A%20%281%29%20how%20to%20reproduce%20the%20issue%2C%20%282%29%20the%20automated%20test%20that%20verifies%20the%20fix%2C%20%283%29%20before/after%20screenshots%20for%20UI%20issues.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20a%20bug%20fix%20does%20not%20have%20a%20reproducing%20test%2C%20treat%20the%20fix%20as%20incomplete%20because%20regressions%20can%20occur%20later%20without%20notice.%0APreparing%20pull%20request.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20code%2C%20follow%20contributing%20guidelines.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20commit%2C%20write%20clear%20message.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20need%20examples%20of%20style%2C%20use%20gh%20pr%20list%20--repo%20link-assistant/%5BREDACTED%5D%20--state%20merged%20--search%20%5Bkeywords%5D.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20open%20pr%2C%20describe%20solution%20draft%20and%20include%20tests.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20there%20is%20a%20package%20with%20version%20and%20GitHub%20Actions%20workflows%20for%20automatic%20release%2C%20update%20the%20version%20in%20your%20pull%20request%20to%20prepare%20for%20next%20release.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20update%20existing%20pr%201583%2C%20use%20gh%20pr%20edit%20to%20modify%20title%20and%20description.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20finalize%20the%20pull%20request%3A%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20check%20that%20the%20pull%20request%20title%20and%20description%20are%20updated%20%28the%20PR%20may%20start%20with%20a%20%5BWIP%5D%20prefix%20and%20a%20placeholder%20description%20that%20should%20be%20replaced%20with%20the%20actual%20title%20and%20description%20of%20the%20changes%29%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20follow%20style%20from%20merged%20prs%20for%20code%2C%20title%2C%20and%20description%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20check%20that%20no%20uncommitted%20changes%20corresponding%20to%20the%20original%20requirements%20are%20left%20behind%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20check%20that%20the%20default%20branch%20is%20merged%20into%20the%20pull%20request%20branch%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20check%20that%20all%20CI%20checks%20are%20passing%20if%20they%20exist%20before%20you%20finish%2C%20including%20checks%20that%20already%20fail%20on%20the%20default%20branch%20%28when%20a%20check%20needs%20a%20human%20action%2C%20make%20CI%20on%20the%20pull%20request%20pass%20without%20it%20and%20CI%20on%20the%20default%20branch%20fail%20with%20an%20explicit%20message%20saying%20what%20to%20do%29%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20check%20for%20latest%20comments%20on%20the%20issue%20and%20pull%20request%20to%20ensure%20no%20recent%20feedback%20was%20missed%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20double-check%20that%20all%20changes%20in%20the%20pull%20request%20address%20the%20original%20requirements%20of%20the%20issue%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20check%20for%20newly%20introduced%20bugs%20in%20the%20pull%20request%20by%20carefully%20reading%20gh%20pr%20diff%2C%0A%20%20%20%20%20%20check%20that%20no%20previously%20existing%20features%20were%20removed%20without%20an%20explicit%20request%20in%20the%20issue%20description%2C%20issue%20comments%2C%20or%20pull%20request%20comments.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20finish%20implementation%2C%20use%20gh%20pr%20ready%201583.%0AWorkflow%20and%20collaboration.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20check%20branch%2C%20verify%20with%20git%20branch%20--show-current.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20push%2C%20push%20only%20to%20branch%20issue-1582-79aa864de807.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20finish%2C%20create%20a%20pull%20request%20from%20branch%20issue-1582-79aa864de807.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20pr%201583%20already%20exists%20for%20this%20branch%2C%20update%20it%20instead%20of%20creating%20new%20one.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20organize%20workflow%2C%20use%20pull%20requests%20instead%20of%20direct%20merges%20to%20default%20branch%20%28main%20or%20master%29.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20manage%20commits%2C%20preserve%20commit%20history%20for%20later%20analysis.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20contribute%2C%20keep%20repository%20history%20forward-moving%20with%20regular%20commits%2C%20pushes%2C%20and%20reverts%20if%20needed.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20face%20conflict%20that%20you%20cannot%20resolve%20yourself%2C%20ask%20for%20help.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20collaborate%2C%20respect%20branch%20protections%20by%20working%20only%20on%20issue-1582-79aa864de807.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20mention%20a%20result%2C%20include%20the%20pull%20request%20URL%20or%20comment%20URL.%0ASelf%20review.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20check%20your%20solution%20draft%2C%20verify%20git%20status%20shows%20a%20clean%20working%20tree%20with%20no%20uncommitted%20changes.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20compare%20with%20repo%20style%2C%20use%20gh%20pr%20diff%20%5Bnumber%5D.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20finalize%2C%20confirm%20code%2C%20tests%2C%20and%20description%20are%20consistent.%0AGitHub%20CLI%20command%20patterns.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20fetching%20lists%20from%20GitHub%20API%2C%20use%20the%20--paginate%20flag%20to%20ensure%20all%20results%20are%20returned%20%28GitHub%20returns%20max%2030%20per%20page%20by%20default%29.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20adding%20PR%20comment%2C%20use%20gh%20pr%20comment%20NUMBER%20--body%20%22text%22%20--repo%20OWNER/REPO.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20adding%20issue%20comment%2C%20use%20gh%20issue%20comment%20NUMBER%20--body%20%22text%22%20--repo%20OWNER/REPO.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20viewing%20PR%20details%2C%20use%20gh%20pr%20view%20NUMBER%20--repo%20OWNER/REPO.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20filtering%20with%20jq%2C%20use%20gh%20api%20repos/link-assistant/%5BREDACTED%5D/pulls/1583/comments%20--paginate%20--jq%20%27reverse%20|%20.%5B0%3A5%5D%27.%0APlaywright%20MCP%20usage%20%28browser%20automation%20via%20MCP%20tools%29.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20develop%20frontend%20web%20applications%20%28HTML%2C%20CSS%2C%20JavaScript%2C%20React%2C%20Vue%2C%20Angular%2C%20etc.%29%2C%20use%20Playwright%20MCP%20tools%20to%20test%20the%20UI%20in%20a%20real%20browser.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20WebFetch%20tool%20fails%20to%20retrieve%20expected%20content%20%28e.g.%2C%20returns%20empty%20content%2C%20JavaScript-rendered%20pages%2C%20or%20login-protected%20pages%29%2C%20use%20Playwright%20MCP%20tools%20%28browser_navigate%2C%20browser_snapshot%29%20as%20a%20fallback%20for%20web%20browsing.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20WebSearch%20tool%20fails%20or%20returns%20insufficient%20results%2C%20use%20Playwright%20MCP%20tools%20%28browser_navigate%2C%20browser_snapshot%29%20as%20a%20fallback%20for%20internet%20search.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20need%20to%20interact%20with%20dynamic%20web%20pages%20that%20require%20JavaScript%20execution%2C%20use%20Playwright%20MCP%20tools.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20need%20to%20visually%20verify%20how%20a%20web%20page%20looks%20or%20take%20screenshots%2C%20use%20browser_take_screenshot%20from%20Playwright%20MCP.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20need%20to%20fill%20forms%2C%20click%20buttons%2C%20or%20perform%20user%20interactions%20on%20web%20pages%2C%20use%20Playwright%20MCP%20tools%20%28browser_click%2C%20browser_type%2C%20browser_fill_form%29.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20need%20to%20test%20responsive%20design%20or%20different%20viewport%20sizes%2C%20use%20browser_resize%20from%20Playwright%20MCP.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20you%20finish%20using%20the%20browser%2C%20close%20it%20with%20browser_close%20to%20free%20resources.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20reproducing%20UI%20bugs%2C%20use%20browser_take_screenshot%20to%20capture%20the%20problem%20state%20before%20implementing%20any%20fix.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20fixing%20UI%20bugs%2C%20take%20before/after%20screenshots%20to%20provide%20visual%20evidence%20of%20the%20fix%20for%20human%20verification.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20creating%20UI%20tests%2C%20save%20baseline%20screenshots%20to%20the%20repository%20for%20visual%20regression%20testing.%0A%20%20%20-%20When%20verifying%20UI%20fixes%2C%20compare%20screenshots%20to%20ensure%20the%20fix%20does%20not%20introduce%20unintended%20visual%20changes.%0AIssue%20completion%20goal.%0A%20%20%20-%20Do%20not%20stop%20until%20every%20requirement%20of%20the%20issue%20and%20all%20required%20sub-issues%20is%20fully%20implemented%20and%20verified%20in%20this%20single%20pull%20request%2C%20in%20the%20widest%20requested%20scope%2C%20with%20no%20requested%20work%20deferred%3B%20work%20that%20is%20truly%20blocked%20must%20be%20reported%20as%20blocked%20and%20left%20unfinished%2C%20never%20presented%20as%20done.%0A%20%20%20-%20Try%20to%20set%20this%20exact%20objective%20with%20a%20native%20goal-setting%20API%20or%20tool%20before%20working%2C%20and%20keep%20it%20active%20until%20every%20acceptance%20criterion%20is%20verified.%20Codex%20exposes%20thread/goal/set%20through%20its%20app-server%20API%20when%20available%3B%20do%20not%20invent%20an%20exec%20--goal%20flag.%20If%20the%20running%20tool%20provides%20no%20native%20goal%20API%2C%20keep%20the%20objective%20and%20checklist%20in%20your%20work%20plan%20across%20turns%20and%20compaction.%0A%20%20%20-%20Read%20the%20complete%20issue%2C%20every%20comment%2C%20every%20required%20sub-issue%2C%20and%20all%20pull%20request%20conversation%20comments%2C%20inline%20comments%2C%20and%20reviews.%20Inventory%20each%20requirement%2C%20including%20prose%20requirements%20and%20later%20feedback%2C%20and%20map%20each%20one%20to%20implementation%20and%20verification%20evidence.%0A%20%20%20-%20Passing%20CI%2C%20a%20partial%20implementation%2C%20an%20upstream%20report%2C%20or%20a%20workaround%20does%20not%20complete%20an%20unmet%20acceptance%20criterion.%20Continue%20authorized%20work.%20If%20an%20external%20blocker%20cannot%20be%20resolved%2C%20report%20the%20exact%20blocked%20criteria%20and%20evidence%2C%20leave%20them%20unfinished%2C%20and%20keep%20the%20pull%20request%20unmerged.%0A%20%20%20-%20Preserve%20a%20positive%20closing%20keyword%20in%20the%20pull%20request%20description%20for%20the%20original%20issue%20and%20every%20required%20issue.%20Repeat%20the%20keyword%20per%20issue%2C%20use%20the%20correct%20repository%20for%20foreign%20issues%2C%20and%20keep%20references%20outside%20examples%20or%20code%20blocks.%20A%20negated%20sentence%20%28for%20example%20%22does%20not%20close%22%20before%20an%20issue%20reference%29%20is%20not%20a%20closing%20reference.%20Mention%20issues%20you%20reported%20to%20other%20repositories%20without%20a%20keyword%3A%20GitHub%20also%20closes%20an%20issue%20linked%20right%20after%20%22fix%3A%22%2C%20as%20in%20%22a%20suggested%20fix%3A%20<issue%20URL>%22.%0ALocation%20privacy%3A%20Keep%20the%20user%27s%20and%20host%27s%20geolocation%20private.%20Avoid%20collecting%2C%20inferring%2C%20or%20transmitting%20their%20location%2C%20including%20IP-geolocation%20lookups%2C%20GPS/browser%20location%20permissions%2C%20local%20timezone%20or%20region%20probes%2C%20and%20user_location%20hints%20in%20search%20or%20model%20requests.%20Use%20location-neutral%20searches.%20Propagate%20this%20policy%20to%20delegated%20agents%20and%20browser/MCP%20tools.%20Locations%20explicitly%20present%20in%20task%20content%20may%20be%20used%20to%20discuss%20that%20content%3B%20they%20do%20not%20authorize%20discovery%20or%20disclosure%20of%20the%20user%27s%20or%20host%27s%20location.%0AIssue%20to%20solve%3A%20https%3A//github.com/link-assistant/%5BREDACTED%5D/issues/1582%0AYour%20prepared%20branch%3A%20issue-1582-79aa864de807%0AYour%20prepared%20working%20directory%3A%20/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1794845157653%0AYour%20prepared%20Pull%20Request%3A%20https%3A//github.com/link-assistant/%5BREDACTED%5D/pull/1583%0ADownload%20all%20logs%20and%20collect%20data%20related%20about%20the%20issue%20to%20this%20repository%2C%20make%20sure%20we%20compile%20that%20data%20into%20the%20./dev/log/issues/1582/pulls/1583%20folder.%0ADo%20not%20stop%20until%20every%20requirement%20of%20the%20issue%20and%20all%20required%20sub-issues%20is%20fully%20implemented%20and%20verified%20in%20this%20single%20pull%20request%2C%20in%20the%20widest%20requested%20scope%2C%20with%20no%20requested%20work%20deferred%3B%20work%20that%20is%20truly%20blocked%20must%20be%20reported%20as%20blocked%20and%20left%20unfinished%2C%20never%20presented%20as%20done.%0AProceed.)) (field role (string user))) (object (field content (string Let%20me%20run%20the%20requested%20command%20to%20get%20that%20for%20you.)) (field role (string assistant)) (field tool_calls (array (object (field function (object (field arguments (string %7B%22command%22%3A%22gh%20issue%20view%20%27https%3A//github.com/link-assistant/%5BREDACTED%5D/issues/1582%27%20--json%20title%20--jq%20.title%20&&%20echo%20&&%20gh%20issue%20view%20%27https%3A//github.com/link-assistant/%5BREDACTED%5D/issues/1582%27%20--json%20body%20--jq%20.body%3B%20printf%20%27%5Cn__formal_ai_exit=%25s%5Cn%27%20%24%3F%22%7D)) (field name (string bash)))) (field id (string call_54fcff76237822d3)) (field type (string function)))))))) (field request_id (string request_602e38be1df4d5c4)) (field timestamp_unix_ms (number 1794845223059))))
(formal-ai-log-v1 (object (field dialog_id (string dialog_1ff7a526a91a7997)) (field messages (array (object (field content (string You%20are%20Agent%2C%20the%20best%20coding%20agent%20on%20the%20planet.%0A%0AYou%20are%20an%20interactive%20CLI%20tool%20that%20helps%20users%20with%20software%20engineering%20tasks.%20Use%20the%20instructions%20below%20and%20the%20tools%20available%20to%20you%20to%20assist%20the%20user.%0A%0AIMPORTANT%3A%20You%20must%20NEVER%20generate%20or%20guess%20URLs%20for%20the%20user%20unless%20you%20are%20confident%20that%20the%20URLs%20are%20for%20helping%20the%20user%20with%20programming.%20You%20may%20use%20URLs%20provided%20by%20the%20user%20in%20their%20messages%20or%20local%20files.%0A%0AIf%20the%20user%20asks%20for%20help%20or%20wants%20to%20give%20feedback%20inform%20them%20of%20the%20following%3A%0A-%20ctrl+p%20to%20list%20available%20actions%0A-%20To%20give%20feedback%2C%20users%20should%20report%20the%20issue%20at%0A%20%20https%3A//github.com/link-assistant/agent%0A%0AWhen%20the%20user%20directly%20asks%20about%20Agent%20%28eg.%20%22can%20Agent%20do...%22%2C%20%22does%20Agent%20have...%22%29%2C%20or%20asks%20in%20second%20person%20%28eg.%20%22are%20you%20able...%22%2C%20%22can%20you%20do...%22%29%2C%20or%20asks%20how%20to%20use%20a%20specific%20Agent%20feature%20%28eg.%20implement%20a%20hook%2C%20write%20a%20slash%20command%2C%20or%20install%20an%20MCP%20server%29%2C%20use%20the%20WebFetch%20tool%20to%20gather%20information%20to%20answer%20the%20question%20from%20Agent%20docs.%20The%20list%20of%20available%20docs%20is%20available%20at%20https%3A//github.com/link-assistant/agent%23readme%0A%0A%23%20Tone%20and%20style%0A-%20Only%20use%20emojis%20if%20the%20user%20explicitly%20requests%20it.%20Avoid%20using%20emojis%20in%20all%20communication%20unless%20asked.%0A-%20Your%20output%20will%20be%20displayed%20on%20a%20command%20line%20interface.%20Your%20responses%20should%20be%20short%20and%20concise.%20You%20can%20use%20Github-flavored%20markdown%20for%20formatting%2C%20and%20will%20be%20rendered%20in%20a%20monospace%20font%20using%20the%20CommonMark%20specification.%0A-%20Output%20text%20to%20communicate%20with%20the%20user%3B%20all%20text%20you%20output%20outside%20of%20tool%20use%20is%20displayed%20to%20the%20user.%20Only%20use%20tools%20to%20complete%20tasks.%20Never%20use%20tools%20like%20Bash%20or%20code%20comments%20as%20means%20to%20communicate%20with%20the%20user%20during%20the%20session.%0A-%20NEVER%20create%20files%20unless%20they%27re%20absolutely%20necessary%20for%20achieving%20your%20goal.%20ALWAYS%20prefer%20editing%20an%20existing%20file%20to%20creating%20a%20new%20one.%20This%20includes%20markdown%20files.%0A%0A%23%20Professional%20objectivity%0APrioritize%20technical%20accuracy%20and%20truthfulness%20over%20validating%20the%20user%27s%20beliefs.%20Focus%20on%20facts%20and%20problem-solving%2C%20providing%20direct%2C%20objective%20technical%20info%20without%20any%20unnecessary%20superlatives%2C%20praise%2C%20or%20emotional%20validation.%20It%20is%20best%20for%20the%20user%20if%20Agent%20honestly%20applies%20the%20same%20rigorous%20standards%20to%20all%20ideas%20and%20disagrees%20when%20necessary%2C%20even%20if%20it%20may%20not%20be%20what%20the%20user%20wants%20to%20hear.%20Objective%20guidance%20and%20respectful%20correction%20are%20more%20valuable%20than%20false%20agreement.%20Whenever%20there%20is%20uncertainty%2C%20it%27s%20best%20to%20investigate%20to%20find%20the%20truth%20first%20rather%20than%20instinctively%20confirming%20the%20user%27s%20beliefs.%0A%0A%23%20Task%20Management%0AYou%20have%20access%20to%20the%20TodoWrite%20tools%20to%20help%20you%20manage%20and%20plan%20tasks.%20Use%20these%20tools%20VERY%20frequently%20to%20ensure%20that%20you%20are%20tracking%20your%20tasks%20and%20giving%20the%20user%20visibility%20into%20your%20progress.%0AThese%20tools%20are%20also%20EXTREMELY%20helpful%20for%20planning%20tasks%2C%20and%20for%20breaking%20down%20larger%20complex%20tasks%20into%20smaller%20steps.%20If%20you%20do%20not%20use%20this%20tool%20when%20planning%2C%20you%20may%20forget%20to%20do%20important%20tasks%20-%20and%20that%20is%20unacceptable.%0A%0AIt%20is%20critical%20that%20you%20mark%20todos%20as%20completed%20as%20soon%20as%20you%20are%20done%20with%20a%20task.%20Do%20not%20batch%20up%20multiple%20tasks%20before%20marking%20them%20as%20completed.%0A%0AExamples%3A%0A%0A<example>%0Auser%3A%20Run%20the%20build%20and%20fix%20any%20type%20errors%0Aassistant%3A%20I%27m%20going%20to%20use%20the%20TodoWrite%20tool%20to%20write%20the%20following%20items%20to%20the%20todo%20list%3A%0A-%20Run%20the%20build%0A-%20Fix%20any%20type%20errors%0A%0AI%27m%20now%20going%20to%20run%20the%20build%20using%20Bash.%0A%0ALooks%20like%20I%20found%2010%20type%20errors.%20I%27m%20going%20to%20use%20the%20TodoWrite%20tool%20to%20write%2010%20items%20to%20the%20todo%20list.%0A%0Amarking%20the%20first%20todo%20as%20in_progress%0A%0ALet%20me%20start%20working%20on%20the%20first%20item...%0A%0AThe%20first%20item%20has%20been%20fixed%2C%20let%20me%20mark%20the%20first%20todo%20as%20completed%2C%20and%20move%20on%20to%20the%20second%20item...%0A..%0A..%0A</example>%0AIn%20the%20above%20example%2C%20the%20assistant%20completes%20all%20the%20tasks%2C%20including%20the%2010%20error%20fixes%20and%20running%20the%20build%20and%20fixing%20all%20errors.%0A%0A<example>%0Auser%3A%20Help%20me%20write%20a%20new%20feature%20that%20allows%20users%20to%20track%20their%20usage%20metrics%20and%20export%20them%20to%20various%20formats%0Aassistant%3A%20I%27ll%20help%20you%20implement%20a%20usage%20metrics%20tracking%20and%20export%20feature.%20Let%20me%20first%20use%20the%20TodoWrite%20tool%20to%20plan%20this%20task.%0AAdding%20the%20following%20todos%20to%20the%20todo%20list%3A%0A1.%20Research%20existing%20metrics%20tracking%20in%20the%20codebase%0A2.%20Design%20the%20metrics%20collection%20system%0A3.%20Implement%20core%20metrics%20tracking%20functionality%0A4.%20Create%20export%20functionality%20for%20different%20formats%0A%0ALet%20me%20start%20by%20researching%20the%20existing%20codebase%20to%20understand%20what%20metrics%20we%20might%20already%20be%20tracking%20and%20how%20we%20can%20build%20on%20that.%0A%0AI%27m%20going%20to%20search%20for%20any%20existing%20metrics%20or%20telemetry%20code%20in%20the%20project.%0A%0AI%27ve%20found%20some%20existing%20telemetry%20code.%20Let%20me%20mark%20the%20first%20todo%20as%20in_progress%20and%20start%20designing%20our%20metrics%20tracking%20system%20based%20on%20what%20I%27ve%20learned...%0A%0A%5BAssistant%20continues%20implementing%20the%20feature%20step%20by%20step%2C%20marking%20todos%20as%20in_progress%20and%20completed%20as%20they%20go%5D%0A</example>%0A%0A%0A%23%20Doing%20tasks%0AThe%20user%20will%20primarily%20request%20you%20perform%20software%20engineering%20tasks.%20This%20includes%20solving%20bugs%2C%20adding%20new%20functionality%2C%20refactoring%20code%2C%20explaining%20code%2C%20and%20more.%20For%20these%20tasks%20the%20following%20steps%20are%20recommended%3A%0A-%20%0A-%20Use%20the%20TodoWrite%20tool%20to%20plan%20the%20task%20if%20required%0A%0A-%20Tool%20results%20and%20user%20messages%20may%20include%20<system-reminder>%20tags.%20<system-reminder>%20tags%20contain%20useful%20information%20and%20reminders.%20They%20are%20automatically%20added%20by%20the%20system%2C%20and%20bear%20no%20direct%20relation%20to%20the%20specific%20tool%20results%20or%20user%20messages%20in%20which%20they%20appear.%0A%0A%0A%23%20Tool%20usage%20policy%0A-%20When%20doing%20file%20search%2C%20prefer%20to%20use%20the%20Task%20tool%20in%20order%20to%20reduce%20context%20usage.%0A-%20You%20should%20proactively%20use%20the%20Task%20tool%20with%20specialized%20agents%20when%20the%20task%20at%20hand%20matches%20the%20agent%27s%20description.%0A%0A-%20When%20WebFetch%20returns%20a%20message%20about%20a%20redirect%20to%20a%20different%20host%2C%20you%20should%20immediately%20make%20a%20new%20WebFetch%20request%20with%20the%20redirect%20URL%20provided%20in%20the%20response.%0A-%20You%20can%20call%20multiple%20tools%20in%20a%20single%20response.%20If%20you%20intend%20to%20call%20multiple%20tools%20and%20there%20are%20no%20dependencies%20between%20them%2C%20make%20all%20independent%20tool%20calls%20in%20parallel.%20Maximize%20use%20of%20parallel%20tool%20calls%20where%20possible%20to%20increase%20efficiency.%20However%2C%20if%20some%20tool%20calls%20depend%20on%20previous%20calls%20to%20inform%20dependent%20values%2C%20do%20NOT%20call%20these%20tools%20in%20parallel%20and%20instead%20call%20them%20sequentially.%20For%20instance%2C%20if%20one%20operation%20must%20complete%20before%20another%20starts%2C%20run%20these%20operations%20sequentially%20instead.%20Never%20use%20placeholders%20or%20guess%20missing%20parameters%20in%20tool%20calls.%0A-%20If%20the%20user%20specifies%20that%20they%20want%20you%20to%20run%20tools%20%22in%20parallel%22%2C%20you%20MUST%20send%20a%20single%20message%20with%20multiple%20tool%20use%20content%20blocks.%20For%20example%2C%20if%20you%20need%20to%20launch%20multiple%20agents%20in%20parallel%2C%20send%20a%20single%20message%20with%20multiple%20Task%20tool%20calls.%0A-%20Use%20specialized%20tools%20instead%20of%20bash%20commands%20when%20possible%2C%20as%20this%20provides%20a%20better%20user%20experience.%20For%20file%20operations%2C%20use%20dedicated%20tools%3A%20Read%20for%20reading%20files%20instead%20of%20cat/head/tail%2C%20Edit%20for%20editing%20instead%20of%20sed/awk%2C%20and%20Write%20for%20creating%20files%20instead%20of%20cat%20with%20heredoc%20or%20echo%20redirection.%20Reserve%20bash%20tools%20exclusively%20for%20actual%20system%20commands%20and%20terminal%20operations%20that%20require%20shell%20execution.%20NEVER%20use%20bash%20echo%20or%20other%20command-line%20tools%20to%20communicate%20thoughts%2C%20explanations%2C%20or%20instructions%20to%20the%20user.%20Output%20all%20communication%20directly%20in%20your%20response%20text%20instead.%0A-%20VERY%20IMPORTANT%3A%20When%20exploring%20the%20codebase%20to%20gather%20context%20or%20to%20answer%20a%20question%20that%20is%20not%20a%20needle%20query%20for%20a%20specific%20file/class/function%2C%20it%20is%20CRITICAL%20that%20you%20use%20the%20Task%20tool%20instead%20of%20running%20search%20commands%20directly.%0A<example>%0Auser%3A%20Where%20are%20errors%20from%20the%20client%20handled%3F%0Aassistant%3A%20%5BUses%20the%20Task%20tool%20to%20find%20the%20files%20that%20handle%20client%20errors%20instead%20of%20using%20Glob%20or%20Grep%20directly%5D%0A</example>%0A<example>%0Auser%3A%20What%20is%20the%20codebase%20structure%3F%0Aassistant%3A%20%5BUses%20the%20Task%20tool%5D%0A</example>%0A%0AIMPORTANT%3A%20Always%20use%20the%20TodoWrite%20tool%20to%20plan%20and%20track%20tasks%20throughout%20the%20conversation.%0A%0A%23%20Code%20References%0A%0AWhen%20referencing%20specific%20functions%20or%20pieces%20of%20code%20include%20the%20pattern%20%60file_path%3Aline_number%60%20to%20allow%20the%20user%20to%20easily%20navigate%20to%20the%20source%20code%20location.%0A%0A<example>%0Auser%3A%20Where%20are%20errors%20from%20the%20client%20handled%3F%0Aassistant%3A%20Clients%20are%20marked%20as%20failed%20in%20the%20%60connectToServer%60%20function%20in%20src/services/process.ts%3A712.%0A</example>%0A)) (field role (string system))) (object (field content (string Here%20is%20some%20useful%20information%20about%20the%20environment%20you%20are%20running%20in%3A%0A<env>%0A%20%20Working%20directory%3A%20/tmp/gh-issue-solver-1794845157653%0A%20%20Is%20directory%20a%20git%20repo%3A%20yes%0A%20%20Platform%3A%20linux%0A%20%20Today%27s%20date%3A%20Mon%20Nov%2016%202026%0A</env>%0A%0A<files>%0A%20%20.cargo/%0A%09audit.toml%0A.githooks/%0A%09pre-commit%0A.github/%0A%09actions/%0A%09%09%5B14%20truncated%5D%0A%09codeql/%0A%09%09%5B1%20truncated%5D%0A%09workflows/%0A%09%09%5B60%20truncated%5D%0A%09actionlint.yaml%0A%09pull_request_template.md%0A%09release-advertisement.json%0A%09zizmor